# Flight profile modules

The mount table is `src/lib/flightProfile/rules.ts`. Change mounts there. Do not hardcode a bay exception in the page.

## Adding a module

1. The id already exists in `MODULE_RULES`. Add a new id there first if it does not.
2. It appears in the picker only when `ready` is true, `photo` is set, and `devices.json` uses the same id.
3. Copy button numbers from the matching handed module. A Space Throttle is not a Modern throttle. A WWII THQ is not the standard THQ.
4. Keyboard and mouse binds stay off the sheets.

## Mounts

- `top` on a stick is the UCM desk mount or a standalone mount. On a throttle it is the module sitting on the throttle. `bottom` is the front, toward the pilot. `left` and `right` are the Gladiator side bus.
- Every bay draws Top, Left, Main, Right, and Bottom. Grey out and disable a mount the selected main does not have.
- A Gladiator exposes top and both side connectors. It has no bottom port.
- An Omni Throttle counts as a throttle. Its elbow closes that side: left-hand keeps the right bus, right-hand keeps the left bus.
- A STECS base has no side bus. The front holder is `bottom`. SEM-V may also sit on `top`.
- A module that can run on its own sits on the top of either side. That top is the UCM desk mount or a standalone mount. This is FSM-GA, SEM, SEM-V, THQ, THQ-V, and ATEM.
- Desktop SEM and THQ also use the side bus. SEM-V and THQ-V also use a throttle's top and its front. On a stick their top does not use the side bus.
- FSM-GA does not use a side connector or the front.
- STEM is a bottom mount on every STECS. ATEM is also a bottom mount on Mini Plus and Max only (`acceptsAtem`).
- A mount holds one module. The same module may be placed on every mount VKB allows. Do not limit a count to one owner's set.
- Two sticks are allowed. Two throttles are not.
- Gunfighter has no side bus. Add it only with a sheet, and only as an overhead main.
